{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins","id":344834,"title":"Alternative Shifter Origins?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T09:22:24-08:00","id":344834,"title":"Alternative Shifter Origins?","content":"So while the WoD setting is pretty awesome, I've never been a fan of the idea that you have to be born as a Lycanthrope, as opposed to being able to become it. I was curious if there were any alternative methods, and if so, what they might include.<br /> <br /> A long time ago, I used to play a game called Shadowbane which had Werewolves, Werebears, and Wererats as obtainable skills. The premise was similar in that Lycanthropes were people who carried the spirits of beasts within them, but instead of it being a type of lineage, it was a skill that anyone with the proper dedication could learn. You dedicate yourself to the animal spirit and commune with it, eventually learning to take on its form. and it grew more powerful with additional training. This means that like WoD, it wasn't a virus that was passed on through infections.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I like this version as it suggests that if someone is willing to take up the burden, they too can walk the border between physical and spiritual, helping to keep the world in balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T10:13:24-08:00","id":344883,"title":"","content":"Well you don't have to be born one in Forsaken, and in 2e you can just be chosen by Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T10:22:44-08:00","id":344889,"title":"","content":"A few different books touch on this to look at. Skinchangers is an entire book on an alternate portrayal of witches who obtain the beast-spirit through a ritual they seek out. War Against the Pure has a chapter about the Uratha discovering and coming into conflict with other changing peoples, including providing for kinds that aren't hereditary, like the roach-men whose rising Primal Urge projects as a side-effect a spiritual infection. And, of course, Forsaken 2e, where the Wolf-Blooded &quot;kin&quot; aren't necessarily a set of bloodlines but also include those touched by the madness of Father Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T16:11:41-08:00","id":345208,"title":"","content":"H:tV has some pretty sweet werewolf alternates, like unions between humans and spirits, or a special five-dot Mystery/Gifted ability which allows you to shapeshift, or the Strange Form power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:52:26-08:00","id":345284,"title":"","content":"Changing breeds has the pretty owod take that shapeshifters are guardians of the earth.<br /> <br /> Blasphemies has alternate origin myths and a hack for for the cinema classic infectious werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T20:42:47-08:00","id":345373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=344889#post344889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few different books touch on this to look at. Skinchangers is an entire book on an alternate portrayal of witches who obtain the beast-spirit through a ritual they seek out. War Against the Pure has a chapter about the Uratha discovering and coming into conflict with other changing peoples, including providing for kinds that aren't hereditary, like the roach-men whose rising Primal Urge projects as a side-effect a spiritual infection. And, of course, Forsaken 2e, where the Wolf-Blooded &quot;kin&quot; aren't necessarily a set of bloodlines but also include those touched by the madness of Father Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Roach&quot; men sound like they would be shit-your-pants terrifying if you encountered one at night!<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with H:tV, what does it stand for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:10:31-08:00","id":345398,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Vigil.<br /> <br /> The roach men are in <i>War Against the Pure</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T01:51:39-08:00","id":345576,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about the who issue of becoming a Werewolf but to me it would make the game to similar to Vampire, Changeling, Mage and other stuff. I kind of like the idea of lineages, family and the brother-against-brother/sister-against-sister theme and all that stuff that goes on in the present Werewolf setting. It makes it easier to feel part of something and in a context for the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T23:09:40-08:00","id":346489,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that people choosing to take up the burden of lycanthropy really jives with WoD. Like, it's supposed to be a terrifying thing where you have to deal with horrible things and die young, along with fighting your own instincts, etc. I kind of think anyone who would choose to be Uratha isn't someone you'd want to meet.<br /> <br /> I do think, though, that it would be interesting if someone or something else chose who became werewolves, to push an agenda of some kind. Maybe Luna picks those who are best suited to police the spirit world, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4473-modestmoussorgsky","name":"ModestMoussorgsky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T23:38:52-08:00","id":346503,"title":"","content":"Die young? From what I've learned, only the spider folk had that problem (5 year life span!). But Werewolves sound like invulnerable killing machines if you give them cause to attack. While I can see what you mean about it being terrifying to go through the First Change with no idea of what's happening, I don't see how that would fit with somebody who voluntarily makes the change. Especially if they know what they're getting into; it could be something along the lines of a Hunter - Shifter fusion. They find out about the spirit world, they find out there are dark and powerful creatures trying to destroy the world. Instead of curling up in the corner waiting to die, these enlightened individuals decide they're going to die with some dignity, and agree to join the fight as one of the people.<br /> <br /> <br /> They're more like heroes than psychologically damaged individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-21-2014, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T07:39:26-08:00","id":346655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ModestMoussorgsky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=346489#post346489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Luna picks those who are best suited to police the spirit world, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the options in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=346503#post346503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're more like heroes than psychologically damaged individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Influencing the Shadow is something any human can do, and one that knows how to see into it can witness the fruits of their work. Why would they need to become a werewolf and constantly deal with death rage, the war against the Pure, literal assault by pretty much every spirit being that exists?<br /> <br /> Simply finding out about the existence of werewolves is one thing, but discovering their mandate seems like it should be an extremely rare event. Actively seeking out the power of others and trying to take it for yourself isn't something heroic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-21-2014, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:55:41-08:00","id":347046,"title":"","content":"It isn't that Uratha have a short lifespan (they can theoretically live much longer than humans), it's that they have a relatively short life expectancy, what with constantly dealing with things that want them dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4473-modestmoussorgsky","name":"ModestMoussorgsky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T05:23:30-08:00","id":347331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=346655#post346655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is one of the options in 2e.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Influencing the Shadow is something any human can do, and one that knows how to see into it can witness the fruits of their work. Why would they need to become a werewolf and constantly deal with death rage, the war against the Pure, literal assault by pretty much every spirit being that exists?<br /> <br /> Simply finding out about the existence of werewolves is one thing, but discovering their mandate seems like it should be an extremely rare event. Actively seeking out the power of others and trying to take it for yourself isn't something heroic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not talking exclusively about werewolves. I did say alternate <i>shifter</i> origins. So I'm asking about any kind of lycanthrope. Sure, the Wolves seem like a pretty grueling task, but the other shifters dedicated themselves to other duties that were less focused on slaughtering everything in sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T12:24:08-08:00","id":347605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=347331#post347331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the other shifters dedicated themselves to other duties that were less focused on slaughtering everything in sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what Forsaken are about.<br /> <br /> What other shifters are you talking about, then? The Unclean and Brinekin don't really have duties, and the Baal-Hadad are horrible in their own way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T18:08:08-08:00","id":347914,"title":"","content":"When I say Shifters, I mean <b>any kind </b>of werebeasts. Like rats, birds, snakes, est. I was asking if there are other types of shifters who don't necessarily have to be descended from some bloodline or ancestry to become one. The books said there could be other breeds besides wolves, so I just use the word Shifter to mean werebeast. Or is that inaccurate for the WoD setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:30:18-08:00","id":347964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books said there could be other breeds besides wolves, so I just use the word Shifter to mean werebeast. </div> </div> </div>There are multiple books detailing &quot;shifters&quot; other than werewolves. Are you thinking of one in particular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4473-modestmoussorgsky","name":"ModestMoussorgsky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:30:59-08:00","id":347965,"title":"","content":"Shifter isn't a particularly useful term within the context of the World of Darkness since there are so many kinds that may or may not be related to each other in any number of ways. Werewolves, which is to say the Uratha, appear to be at least somewhat unique from other kinds of animal-themed shapeshifters in the details of their relationship with the Shadow and its denizens.<br /> <br /> Long story short, if you're playing a Werebear from the Changing Breeds book or one of the Brinekin from the back of War Against the Pure, you're not playing a Werewolf with the wolf bit exchanged for some other animal. You're playing a potentially different entity entirely. I say potentially because while there are myths and legends, there is no canonical story of their origins. <br /> <br /> For instance, the mainstream Uratha legend concerning their origin is that they're the offspring of Urfarah the wolf god and Luna in human form. Well as far as anyone can tell, that's not where Werebears come from so either that story isn't true (read: likely) or Werebears have a completely different origin (read: also likely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T21:01:44-08:00","id":347976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=347965#post347965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For instance, the mainstream Uratha legend concerning their origin is that they're the offspring of Urfarah the wolf god and Luna in human form. Well as far as anyone can tell, that's not where Werebears come from so either that story isn't true (read: likely) or Werebears have a completely different origin (read: also likely).</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, there is the implication that the Wayward Sons from WATP bear some relation to Luna, considering their susceptibility to silver and Rage, and the line from the corebook about how Luna cursed &quot;all the children she had ever borne.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T23:21:13-08:00","id":348055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=347976#post347976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although, there is the implication that the Wayward Sons from WATP bear some relation to Luna, considering their susceptibility to silver and Rage, and the line from the corebook about how Luna cursed &quot;all the children she had ever borne.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All the werebeasts in Changing Breeds have a vulnerability to silver as well for ambiguous reasons. In fact they're more susceptible to it than Forsaken, yet mechanically different to that of the Pure. There's a vague implication that maybe it's because of some rivalry between the Moon and the Earth (the latter of which is fairly foreign to Forsaken as a whole, yet drenches the Changing Breeds book), but nothing solid or canonical.<br /> <br /> There's even a breed of werewolf changing breeds called the Vargr, or Forgotten Ones. Their entry starts off with a snippet about having no ties to Father Wolf and claiming none, then towards the end mentions that while they can turn into a dire wolf they lack a war-form and implies that Father Wolf's 'favored' progeny inherited that alone.<br /> <br /> There are lots of implications, there is no hard canon. That said Changing Breeds isn't particularly well known for its consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T03:53:48-08:00","id":348153,"title":"","content":"Go read Changing Breeds again then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:54:13-08:00","id":348244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=347965#post347965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifter isn't a particularly useful term within the context of the World of Darkness since there are so many kinds that may or may not be related to each other in any number of ways. Werewolves, which is to say the Uratha, appear to be at least somewhat unique from other kinds of animal-themed shapeshifters in the details of their relationship with the Shadow and its denizens.<br /> <br /> Long story short, if you're playing a Werebear from the Changing Breeds book or one of the Brinekin from the back of War Against the Pure, you're not playing a Werewolf with the wolf bit exchanged for some other animal. You're playing a potentially different entity entirely. I say potentially because while there are myths and legends, there is no canonical story of their origins.<br /> <br /> For instance, the mainstream Uratha legend concerning their origin is that they're the offspring of Urfarah the wolf god and Luna in human form. Well as far as anyone can tell, that's not where Werebears come from so either that story isn't true (read: likely) or Werebears have a completely different origin (read: also likely).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, I thought the Weres were all in the same boat (guarding the spirit world), just dedicated to different tasks. But if they have different creation myths, then I could see how different origin concepts would be possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Changing Breeds sounds like a good concept idea book, and even if the mechanics for the game are utterly broken as described <a href=\"http://destroythis.blogspot.com/2014/07/intro.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, I'm still considering getting it at some point for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T10:52:44-08:00","id":348423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=348244#post348244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, I thought the Weres were all in the same boat (guarding the spirit world), just dedicated to different tasks. But if they have different creation myths, then I could see how different origin concepts would be possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Changing Breeds sounds like a good concept idea book, and even if the mechanics for the game are utterly broken as described <a href=\"http://destroythis.blogspot.com/2014/07/intro.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, I'm still considering getting it at some point for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. The execution is terrible, but the good news is that the amount of salvageable material in there makes for good ways to waste time on sleepless nights.<br /> <br /> (Well, except for the were-elephants. Those stump me.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887