attered on impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T04:46:05-08:00","id":359011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/344834-alternative-shifter-origins?p=348244#post348244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I thought the Weres were all in the same boat (guarding the spirit world), just dedicated to different tasks. But if they have different creation myths, then I could see how different origin concepts would be possible.<br /> <br /> I think Changing Breeds sounds like a good concept idea book, and even if the mechanics for the game are utterly broken as described <a href=\"http://destroythis.blogspot.com/2014/07/intro.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, I'm still considering getting it at some point for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be better if Weres had their own niche and their own spirit patrons. War against the Pure handled them fantastically (mostly the lot of them use methods other than bloodline, infection being a few) but those shifters were limited on Shadow matters.<br /> <br /> Shame CB took WtA's angle and crammed it into WtF. WtF (or even the nWoD line in general) doesn't have the 80's &quot;Fuck you! I got mine!&quot; cutthroat capitalism feel that WtA has instead of working with a more local, city wide, investigative feel. It's like having members of Earth First showing up in the 3rd season of The Wire and you're left wondering what the hell are they doing there and how these hippy looking motherfuckers haven't been shot yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}